ution through state policies. For more information about\nhealth impacts and how ozone pollution forms in Colorado, visit:\nhttps://cdphe.colorado.gov/ozone- pollution-and-your-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion.","ends":"2026-08-28T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Broomfield, CO; Jefferson, CO; Denver, CO; Douglas, CO; Adams, CO; Boulder, CO; Weld, CO; Larimer, CO; Arapahoe, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a17a27b506afd523954d57cd2deb7b4d9d4ce26d.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a17a27b506afd523954d57cd2deb7b4d9d4ce26d.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-28T19:30:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 281930 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 130 PM MDT Fri Aug 28 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Isolated/scattered high based showers/storms this afternoon/evening with gusty winds. - Temperatures return to the 90s today and Saturday across the plains. - Thunderstorm coverage increases for late Saturday through Monday. && .DISCUSSION /Through Friday/","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-28T19:52:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Saturday... Above-normal temperatures are expected today and Saturday, with scattered high-based showers and storms capable of producing gusty outflows/microbursts each afternoon. Flow aloft is expected to bring some gusty winds (25-30 mph) into North Park both days that will lead to elevated fire weather conditions, but RH is expected to remain above critical t","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"}